A||||4||HYPTNOTiSE||Got my new headers!!! got pics too.||||1||
Z||000000||HYPTNOTiSE||08-12-2000||03:16 PM||||They're just in cheezy black paint right now, so they wont rust. I'm going to have them thermal coated on monday in a bright shiny silver finsh inside and out.  1.5 inch primarys, 15 inch long, to  2.25 collectors, to a 2.25 inch crossover pipe, and where the two peices of crossover pipe meet it becomes 2.5 inch. They're TIG welded inside and out, and are super clean and well built. I still need to get header studs and copper collector gaskets. shouldn't be to big a problem.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieropage/headers3.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieropage/headers4.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieropage/crossover.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieropage/headersetup.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||08-12-2000||04:53 PM||||Where did you get those?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Patrick||08-12-2000||07:51 PM||||<BR>Is the need for a crossover pipe because you have to run a cat?<P>A <I>true</I> dual-exhaust with two separate mufflers would be nice with those headers! ||||reg||5
Z||000003||1FST2M6||08-12-2000||08:54 PM||||make sure you run on a dyno before you put them on and after... ||||reg||1
Z||000004||HYPTNOTiSE||08-13-2000||12:31 PM||||I wish i could run on a dyno before and after but time complications aren't going to alow that. My new engine/tranny/cradle is going in about 3-4 weeks.  These headers are very tricky to install, and i dont plan on installing them in the car, they're getting installed out of the car while the cradle is removed and i have a place to work.  I dont want to run a dual exhuast because that would be over 1000 dollars extra. I will only run stainless exhuast( i hate rust! i've had old cars in the past and i work on old cars a lot) and i will only run mandrel bent tubing.  Dont know if anyone has checked lately but they're are no mandrel tubing benders in the state of maryland.  Also if I went out of state to have the work done, they all want everything on paper with drawings and dimensions. No thanks. I already have the borla exhuast. I think this combo should sound awesome. Once upon a time i had a set of equal length long tube headers. I sold them to a guy named doug chase.  The tubes were 36 inches long! But they were bent for an auto.  With that setup you would have to run dual exhuast. Also if you were going to run true dual exhuast, you'd have to figure out where to put the O2 sensor.  these headers follow the stock stuff as much as possible. very nice quality. I have to have a custom downpipe made to mate with the rest of my exhuast. It will be 2.5 inch and will have a cat on it. But it will be easy to take off, and i'm also going to have a downpipe with no cat on it for anytime other than emissions day.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
